  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41161590",
      "title": "Adding a Backend to the React SPA",
      "lectureOrder": 34,
      "videoOrder": 32,
      "sourceHash": "da7034ea6ef5a4919fd6ef81620970806da411d145f9c3176b5a4c6a82a021ff",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 3.42,
          "en": "By now, we learned a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.42,
          "end": 7.83,
          "en": "about the most essential React features you must know to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.83,
          "end": 12.83,
          "en": "get started building Reactive user interfaces with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.87,
          "end": 17.7,
          "en": "But the demo app, the demo website we built thus far",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 20.673,
          "en": "of course only works in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.399,
          "end": 27.15,
          "en": "There It works absolutely fine, but if we add posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 27.15,
          "end": 31.05,
          "en": "and we then reload this site, all the data is lost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 31.05,
          "end": 34.44,
          "en": "because at the moment it's only stored in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 34.44,
          "end": 38.49,
          "en": "whilst this React app, this JavaScript app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 38.49,
          "end": 41.55,
          "en": "in the end is running in React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 41.55,
          "end": 42.99,
          "en": "And that's really important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.99,
          "end": 46.65,
          "en": "is a frontend JavaScript library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.65,
          "end": 49.59,
          "en": "You use it to build a user interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.59,
          "end": 54.27,
          "en": "It powers your web user interface with JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 54.27,
          "end": 58.86,
          "en": "in the end, and it therefore executes in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 58.86,
          "end": 63.12,
          "en": "Indeed, what we're building with ReactJS in most cases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 63.12,
          "end": 68.12,
          "en": "is a so-called single page application and application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 68.34,
          "end": 73.34,
          "en": "a website where we in the end have only one single HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 73.38,
          "end": 77.13,
          "en": "this index html file here, and then everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 77.13,
          "end": 80.85,
          "en": "that happens on the screen is powered by JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 80.85,
          "end": 84.27,
          "en": "So if we open a model here, that's not a new page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 84.27,
          "end": 88.35,
          "en": "not a new HTML file that's being downloaded or opened.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 88.35,
          "end": 91.38,
          "en": "Instead it's the existing page being edited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 91.38,
          "end": 96.38,
          "en": "by JavaScript the DOM being edited by JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 101.34,
          "en": "If I view this page source here, I just see the basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 101.34,
          "end": 106.05,
          "en": "empty HTML file, this index html file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 106.05,
          "end": 108.53999999999999,
          "en": "that was downloaded initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 108.53999999999999,
          "end": 111.96000000000001,
          "en": "But in this file we have this script import, which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 111.96000000000001,
          "end": 116.61,
          "en": "in the end imports our Java script, our React application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 116.61,
          "end": 120.72,
          "en": "and its stat application that then edits the DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 120.72,
          "end": 124.92,
          "en": "so that the actually rendered DOM has far more elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 124.92,
          "end": 127.59,
          "en": "than the initial HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 127.59,
          "end": 131.61,
          "en": "So we use React to build this interactive front end, and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 131.61,
          "end": 135.48,
          "en": "in the end what we're building is a single page application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 135.48,
          "end": 139.68,
          "en": "But it would of course be nice if the posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 139.68,
          "end": 143.19,
          "en": "that we create here would not just be stored locally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 143.19,
          "end": 146.82,
          "en": "in memory so that they're lost whenever we reload this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 146.82,
          "end": 150.72,
          "en": "and so that also no other users can see them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 150.72,
          "end": 153.84,
          "en": "But if we instead had some backend to which we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 153.84,
          "end": 157.38,
          "en": "can send requests and from which we get back responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 157.38,
          "end": 161.91,
          "en": "where the data could then be stored in a actual database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 161.91,
          "end": 165.96,
          "en": "So with backend, I mean a separate web application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 165.96,
          "end": 170.96,
          "en": "a web api, rest api, for example, running on some server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 171.39,
          "end": 174.99,
          "en": "so not in the browser of our users, but on some server owned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 174.99,
          "end": 178.35,
          "en": "by us, for example, and that backend api,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 178.35,
          "end": 182.16,
          "en": "that rest API could be built with any language",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 182.16,
          "end": 186.48,
          "en": "or framework of your choice, not necessarily with JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 186.48,
          "end": 190.32,
          "en": "and typically not with React, since React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 190.32,
          "end": 195.03,
          "en": "is not really a backend library, I'm saying not really",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 195.03,
          "end": 199.26,
          "en": "because there are frameworks like Next JS or Remix",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 199.26,
          "end": 204.09,
          "en": "on which I also got courses that build up on top of React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 204.09,
          "end": 208.71,
          "en": "and allow you to blend backend code into your React app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 208.71,
          "end": 212.19,
          "en": "But React itself is not a backend library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 212.19,
          "end": 215.37,
          "en": "Instead, it really focuses on allowing you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 215.37,
          "end": 219.03,
          "en": "to build interactive user interfaces as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 219.03,
          "end": 221.57999999999998,
          "en": "But we still might want to be able to store data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 221.57999999999998,
          "end": 224.46,
          "en": "on some backend, in some database, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 224.46,
          "end": 226.92000000000002,
          "en": "And for that we need such a backend api",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 226.92000000000002,
          "end": 230.5,
          "en": "either a third party API or an API built by us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 231.39,
          "end": 235.05,
          "en": "and then that api, that backend service could interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 235.05,
          "end": 237.63,
          "en": "with files or with databases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 237.63,
          "end": 241.59,
          "en": "or anything like that so that our frontend application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 241.59,
          "end": 244.83,
          "en": "the React app then can send HTTP requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 244.83,
          "end": 248.04,
          "en": "to the backend so that some data gets stored there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 248.04,
          "end": 251.25,
          "en": "or so that we fetch some data from the backend which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 251.25,
          "end": 255.87,
          "en": "is then returned to the frontend through an HTTP response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 255.87,
          "end": 259.77,
          "en": "That is something we might want for this demo app here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 259.77,
          "end": 262.26,
          "en": "And for that reason attached you find a link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 262.26,
          "end": 266.49,
          "en": "to a dummy backend project, a dummy rest API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 266.49,
          "end": 269.64,
          "en": "in the end built with Node and Express JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 269.64,
          "end": 271.71,
          "en": "So no React code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 271.71,
          "end": 274.29,
          "en": "and you don't need to know node or express to follow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 274.29,
          "end": 278.169,
          "en": "along because this backend API is already finished.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 278.169,
          "end": 279.69,
          "en": "And what I'm doing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 279.69,
          "end": 282.81,
          "en": "in this backend API is I'm storing some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 282.81,
          "end": 285.12,
          "en": "in a post dot JSON file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 285.12,
          "end": 286.77,
          "en": "We could also use a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 286.77,
          "end": 289.32,
          "en": "but that would simply require some extra setup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 289.32,
          "end": 290.73,
          "en": "So for this demo, I'm just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 290.73,
          "end": 293.15999999999997,
          "en": "using this file we're storing some data there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 293.15999999999997,
          "end": 295.65,
          "en": "and we're fetching some data from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 295.65,
          "end": 298.68,
          "en": "And I provide various REST API endpoints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 298.68,
          "end": 303.3,
          "en": "that allow us to get a single post or create a new post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 303.3,
          "end": 304.68,
          "en": "And then I got all the logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 304.68,
          "end": 307.89,
          "en": "for doing those tasks in here in this api.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 307.89,
          "end": 311.34,
          "en": "And therefore if we start this backend server locally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 311.34,
          "end": 314.22,
          "en": "on our machine for this demo, we can add code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 314.22,
          "end": 317.46,
          "en": "to this frontend application to this React application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 317.46,
          "end": 320.4,
          "en": "for it to reach out to this backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 320.4,
          "end": 321.57,
          "en": "And of course, if you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 321.57,
          "end": 324.48,
          "en": "would deploy this you would have two different servers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 324.48,
          "end": 326.16,
          "en": "with two different domains.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 326.16,
          "end": 328.56,
          "en": "Here we can run both on our local machine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 328.56,
          "end": 332.01,
          "en": "and simply use different ports to simulate different servers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 332.01,
          "end": 333.65999999999997,
          "en": "and domains.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 333.65999999999997,
          "end": 335.44,
          "en": "This backend application listens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 336.469,
          "end": 339.45,
          "en": "on port 8080 and we can start it by first of all, running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 339.45,
          "end": 342.57,
          "en": "NPM install to install all dependencies that are required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 342.57,
          "end": 346.29,
          "en": "and then running NPM start to start that node server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 346.29,
          "end": 349.2,
          "en": "And just as the front end development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 349.2,
          "end": 351.78,
          "en": "you should keep that server up and running as long",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 351.78,
          "end": 354.903,
          "en": "as you wanna be able to send requests to this backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 356.1,
          "end": 357.869,
          "en": "So now with that back at up and running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 357.869,
          "end": 359.94,
          "en": "we can go back to the front end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 359.94,
          "end": 362.01,
          "en": "and add some code to it that allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 362.01,
          "end": 365.7,
          "en": "to send requests to that back and to create new posts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 365.7,
          "end": 368.283,
          "en": "and of course to fetch posts as well.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
